Z||000011||mrfiero||03-12-2001||01:06 PM||||JB,<P>I'll take another look at it today and will get back with you.  To be honest, I really didn't look at it very hard.....as soon as I got it I left for California (just got back yesterday).       <P>I can tell you that it is bright red with tan interior, auto., air, cruise, tilt, pw, pdl, hardtop.  It has 14" wheels and a Firebird style spoiler (I have no idea what happened to the original stuff).  The left rear caliper is seized, so it really isn't driveable right now (I plan on putting on a good caliper though), the steering column has the "wobble" (will fix this too), the interior is fair......not too bad, but not perfect either.  It has high miles, but was pretty well cared for......it shows 191K miles.  <P>I'll take a good look at it today and wil try to take a few pictures too. <P><BR>Fiero64,<P>I love silver too.  My favorite color is black, but silver has really grown in me.  Besides, it is a "rare" '88 color......only 261 Formulas came in silver!  Silver is the lowest produced Formula color (next closest is yellow with 436) and I believe I have the lowest mileage silver Formula too (although there may be a lower mileage one out there).<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 03-12-2001).]||||reg||1
